Z||000000||HotFiero||10-16-2001||11:50 AM||||<BR>I own a 86 Fiero SE. I can not get my hood open. I pull the handle and feel usuall tension but it wont pop up. I am lost I tried pulling on it . I sparyed it with WD-40. I am afraid of also cracking my windshield if i try to pry it open. Can someone help. I know I gonna get a flat and be stuck. <P>------------------<BR><BR>Michael||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-16-2001||12:03 PM||||Have somebody push down over the latch and pull the release handle. I trashed a hood with the same problem! Had it down to the latch and gave it one last tug, at the same time my son leaned across the hood for a tool and it popped open!<BR>Try it!||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||10-16-2001||01:28 PM||||If all else fails, I have designed a tool to help Ausfiero out when he broke both release cables.  You could build the tool to release the hood. Go to this thread to get my instructions.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-008917.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20010924-2-008917.html</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-16-2001||05:08 PM||||no one said, did you know theres 2 cables? U may have gotten something in there and closed it down and its putting too much pressure on the latch too. When you do get it open, be sure to WD40 it and grease with lithium grease.||||reg||1
